  "candidate_letter": "Dear Recruiter,\n\nThe candidate has demonstrated strong experience in Python-based web development, including building multiple large-scale systems such as web stores and multilingual websites, and has hands-on experience with AWS, Docker, and CI/CD pipelines. However, they do not meet the mandatory requirement of having experience with asynchronous programming and performance-critical applications, which is essential for this Python Backend Developer role. This missing requirement is the primary reason for the rejection.\n\nWhile the candidate has experience with AWS, Docker, and microservices, and has worked with FastAPI and containerized deployments, there is no evidence of work involving asynchronous programming (e.g., async/await, event loops, or performance optimization in high-concurrency environments).\n\nWe recommend not proceeding with this candidate for the role, as the absence of asynchronous programming experience directly contradicts a core technical requirement. Further evaluation of candidates with proven experience in asynchronous systems and performance-critical backend development is advised.\n\nBest regards,\nAutomated Screening System",
